WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.563
Missing information is a design choice not

00:00:02.576 --> 00:00:07.021
something we should leave accidental NULL represents

00:00:07.035 --> 00:00:11.235
unknown missing or not-applicable information It is

00:00:11.261 --> 00:00:13.024
not the same as zero an empty

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:17.402
string or false For each column ask

00:00:17.428 --> 00:00:21.858
whether missingness makes sense A patient medical

00:00:21.884 --> 00:00:24.068
record number may be required so it

00:00:24.094 --> 00:00:27.097
should not be nullable Email may be

00:00:27.123 --> 00:00:30.610
optional An appointment start time is required

00:00:30.637 --> 00:00:34.123
for a scheduled appointment A cancellation time

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:35.926
only makes sense when an appointment is

00:00:35.939 --> 00:00:39.658
cancelled so it may be nullable A

00:00:39.671 --> 00:00:43.463
data dictionary documents these decisions It should

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:46.635
describe the column meaning type nullability units

00:00:46.792 --> 00:00:51.852
keys and important business rules This documentation

00:00:51.878 --> 00:00:55.010
helps future analysts interpret the database
correctly
